WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.500
PathBlender blends each team's route files into one field view.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.000
Both teams' exported files are processed locally in the browser.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.500
Two robots appear, and the conflict check reports 1.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.000
Press Play to move both robots on one shared clock.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.500
Pause anywhere to inspect a single moment.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.000
The checks panel lists each conflict moment.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.500
Click an entry to jump the clock right to it.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.000
"Try an example" loads three real robots with routes.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.500
The conflict check reports 3.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:51.000
"Arrange timeline" swaps in another route from the library.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:57.500
The check goes from 3 to 1; swapping back restores 3.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:03.000
"Mirror left/right" flips robot 11019 to the mirrored side.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.500
The check goes from 3 to 2.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:15.500
Switch the whole session red or blue: verdicts stay the same.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.000
The analysis view never rewrites your original files or robot programs.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.500
Learn more in Help → Quick guide.
